          <td class="News"><a title="hybrid-d77 is a proof-of-concept distribution based on Chimera Linux, a project that combines the Linux kernel with the BSD userland (FreeBSD's chimerautils) and the APK package manager from Alpine Linux. Hence the reason for the word &quot;hybrid&quot; in the distribution's name - it refers to the unusual fusion of various BSD and Linux components the result of which is a unique, hybrid operating system. The project offers two separate live images that feature either the niri compositor with the custom-built Utumno desktop shell (a Quickshell fork) or the Sway compositor with a Waybar bar. hybrid-d77 uses the Dinit init system and provides two system installation programs, a command-line one as well as a graphical installation tool called &quot;Mocinha&quot;." href="hybridd77">hybrid-d77</a> &bull; <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/hybrid-d77/files/hybrid-d77-live-x86_64-20261113-niri.iso">20261113</a></td>
