        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-11</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="deepin (formerly, Deepin, Linux Deepin, Hiweed GNU/Linux) is a Debian-based distribution (it was Ubuntu-based until version 15 released in late 2015) that aims to provide an elegant, user-friendly and reliable operating system. It does not only include the best the open source world has to offer, but it has also created its own desktop environment called DDE or Deepin Desktop Environment which is based on the Qt 5 toolkit. Deepin focuses much of its attention on intuitive design. Its home-grown applications, like Deepin Software Centre, DMusic and DPlayer are tailored to the average user. Being easy to install and use, deepin can be a good Windows alternative for office and home use." href="deepin">deepin</a> &bull; <a href="https://cdimage.deepin.com/releases/25.3.0/amd64/deepin-desktop-community-25.3.0-amd64.iso">25.3.0</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-11</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="RuscaLinux is a desktop Linux distribution based on Debian's &quot;Stable&quot; branch and featuring the GNOME desktop. The project's goal is to provide a complete, ready-to-go desktop with a curated software set, but without any update mechanisms. This is the distribution's deliberate design choice; it provides no live repositories so the system stays exactly as installed and tested, and any new versions arrive as fresh ISO images. It is a stability-first model, similar in spirit to immutable distributions but reached through a different path." href="ruscalinux">RuscaLinux</a> &bull; <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/ruscalinux/files/1.99.2/ruscalinux-1.99.2-amd64.hybrid.iso">1.99.2</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-10</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="KLV-Airedale is an independently-developed, general-purpose and minimalist Linux distribution featuring a customised Xfce desktop. It is compatible with Void, as it uses Void's package management tools and repositories. The distribution is built using a custom build script called FirstRib, which deploys the OverlayFS filesystem to provide a frugal install, Squashfs capabilities, and an option to copy the system to RAM (copy2ram). Like Void, KLV-Airedale uses the runit init system." href="klv">KLV-Airedale</a> &bull; <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/klv-airedale/files/sr23/KLV-Airedale-sr23.iso">sr23</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-10</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="Unraid OS is a Linux-based commercial operating system designed to provide an easy-to-use and flexible platform for building and managing a Network-Attached Storage (NAS). Some of Unraid's main features include the ability to mix and match drives of different sizes, an easy-to-use web interface for managing storage, virtual machines and Docker containers, protection to safeguard against drive failures, ability to expand the storage by adding more drives." href="unraid">Unraid</a> &bull; <a href="https://releases.unraid.net/dl/stable/7.4.0/5d32b11ee717f3bcc946145606b84cea85fc8cf6d0eb63c2b66649984b6817c7/unRAIDServer-7.4.0-x86_64.zip">7.4.0</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-10</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="Talos is a specialist Linux-based operating system for running Kubernetes, an open-source system for automating deployment, scaling and management of containerised applications. Minimal, immutable and hardened, it does not offer any shell or interactive console; instead, all system management is done via remote Application Programming Interface (API) calls, where messages sent from a client application are protected with mutual Transport Layer Security TLS (mTLS) authentication. Talos also delivers atomic updates, thus maintaining the Linux and Kubernetes versions up-to-date. Talos is developed in the USA by Sidero Labs, Inc." href="talos">Talos</a> &bull; <a href="https://github.com/siderolabs/talos/releases/download/v1.15.0-beta.0/metal-amd64.iso">1.15.0-beta0</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-10</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="XXRI OS is an ultra lightweight desktop Linux distribution designed specifically for older and low-specification computers, including 32-bit systems. It features a custom desktop, called XXRI, which strives to be modern and polished, and which does not require the use of terminal for most common tasks. It also provides a set of custom applications, including XXRI Browser, XXRI File and XXRI Media, as well as a comprehensive graphical control centre called XXRI Settings. Although the distribution does not offer any traditional package manager, additional applications can be installed through XXRI Store, an online repository of popular open-source software." href="xxri">XXRI</a> &bull; <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/xxri-os-lite/files/XXRI-OS-Lite-2.7/XXRI-Lite-2.7-64bit.iso">2.7</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-10</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="NethSecurity is a full-featured open-source Linux firewall that streamlines network security deployment in just a few clicks. NethSecurity is a spin-off of the <a href=&quot;nethserver&quot;>NethServer</a> project. It combines multiple security features into a single platform including firewalling, intrusion detection and prevention, antivirus, multi-WAN, DNS and content filtering." href="nethsecurity">NethSecurity</a> &bull; <a href="https://updates.nethsecurity.nethserver.org/stable/8.8.1/targets/x86/64/nethsecurity-8.8.1-x86-64-generic-squashfs-combined-efi.img.gz">8.8.1</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-10</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="BashCore is a Debian-based live Linux distribution designed for security professionals, networking enthusiasts and students. It is available in several editions. The original BashCore is a minimalist command-line only product based on Debian's &quot;Oldstable&quot; branch, while BashCoreX comes with the Xfce desktop, several privacy-oriented web browsers and other productivity tools. BashCoreZ, BashCoreT and BashCoreTX, based on Debian &quot;Stable&quot;, are editions that range from ultra-minimal to a complete Xfce desktop. There are also BashLabOS and BashCoreGee, two general-purpose distributions for everyday use, with either Xfce or GNOME, and with various productivity applications, including GIMP, LibreOffice and several web browsers. The distribution also includes Tor and other privacy tools." href="bashcore">BashCore</a> &bull; <a href="https://www.bashcore.org/downloads/BashCore2611-Jeff.iso">2611</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-10</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="ChurrOS is an Arch-based, rolling-release Linux distribution for the desktop. It defaults to the Spanish language, offering a choice of two user interfaces - a traditional Xfce desktop with a Whisker menu, or a tiling niri compositor with a custom Waybar bar and the fuzzel applications launcher. It also provides several utilities developed in-house and written in Rust; these include Churros Welcome, Churros Settings, Churros Control Center and Churros Popup. The objective of the project is to build a modern, fast and elegant Linux distribution with its proper identity, branding and useful configuration tools." href="churros">ChurrOS</a> &bull; <a href="https://download.churroslinux.org/ChurrOS-1.5-xfce-x86_64.iso">1.5</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-09</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="EasyOS is an experimental Linux distribution which uses many of the technologies and package formats pioneered by Puppy Linux. The distribution features custom container technology called Easy Containers which can run applications or the entire desktop environment in a container. Packages, desktop settings, networking and sharing resources over the network can all be controlled through graphical utilities." href="easyos">EasyOS</a> &bull; <a href="https://distro.ibiblio.org/easyos/amd64/releases/excalibur/2026/7.5.1/easy-7.5.1-amd64.img">7.5.1</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-09</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="ArchBang Linux is a lightweight distribution based on Arch Linux. Using the labwc Wayland compositor, it is fast, up-to-date and suitable for both desktop and portable systems. Besides GreenBANG, the project also develops a distribution called SwayBang featuring the Sway Wayland compositor." href="archbang">ArchBANG</a> &bull; <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/archbang/files/ArchBANG/archbang-091126-x86_64.iso">091126</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-09</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="Besgnulinux is a lightweight, desktop Linux distribution based on Debian's &quot;stable&quot; branch. Using the JWM window manager, it is designed to be fast, lightweight and easy to use, suitable for older and low-specification computers. Besgnulinux comes with the Calamares system installer, the Brave web browser, and over 40 custom-built tools to control the systems settings as well as the desktop's look-and-feel." href="besgnulinux">Besgnulinux</a> &bull; <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/besgnulinux/files/besgnulinux-jwm-4.2.iso">4.2</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-08</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="ZelixOS is an Arch-based, rolling-release Linux distribution featuring the KDE Plasma desktop in live mode. It is developed with a focus on gaming, software development and high-performance computing. Some of the key features of the distribution include a custom Python/PyQt6 graphical installation wizard called &quot;Zelix Installer&quot;, an ability to choose a preferred desktop environment or Wayland compositor during installation, a post-installation welcome screen called &quot;Zelix Hello&quot;, support for the Steam gaming platform, and various performance tweaks." href="zelixos">ZelixOS</a> &bull; <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/zelixos/files/zelix_isos/zelixos-2026.11.07-x86_64.iso">2026.11.07</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-08</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="NagisinnraLinux is a Japanese Linux distribution based on Debian's &quot;Stable&quot; branch. Featuring a lightweight Xfce desktop, it is specifically designed to revive older hardware and provide a snappy and minimal, yet fully functional desktop environment for daily use. The distribution's main features include out-of-the-box support for the Japanese language, advanced memory optimisation, use of zram compression to guarantee smooth multitasking, and removal of unnecessary and redundant services to maximise battery life and CPU responsiveness." href="nagisinnra">NagisinnraLinux</a> &bull; <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/nagisinnralinux/files/NagisinnraLinux-KDE/NagisinnraLinux-KDE-v1.0.3.iso">1.0.3</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-08</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="TTOS Linux is a desktop-oriented Linux distribution based on Debian's &quot;Stable&quot; branch. It comes with several custom utilities and features, such as a user-friendly Internet security suite, an animated live wallpaper, NVIDIA GPU support, a ClamAV antivirus suite, Android remote messaging, UEFI support, and a net system installer with a choice of multiple desktop environments." href="ttos">TTOS</a> &bull; <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/ttos-linux/files/Release1.3.x/TTOS-1.3.0-Detroit.20261106.iso">20261106</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-08</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="GNUSlashLinux is an Arch-based, rolling-release Linux distribution featuring the minimalist Noctalia desktop shell on top of the niri Wayland compositor. It is designed specifically for developers and power users seeking a lean, keyboard-driven operating system. The distribution's default software set includes a GPU-accelerated Kitty terminal, the modern Helix text editor, the asynchronous Yazi terminal file manager, the privacy-focused Helium web browser, and the Zathura document viewer. GNUSlashLinux also provides several pre-configured themes and colour schemes, as well as various modern command-line tools as alternatives to classic Unix commands." href="gnuslashlinux">GNUSlashLinux</a> &bull; <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/gnuslashlinux/files/GNUSlashLinux_20261108_Final.iso">20261108</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-08</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="Helwan Linux is an Arch-based Linux distribution designed for home, education and development use. Its &quot;Home&quot; flavour comes with the GNOME desktop, the &quot;Edu&quot; variant ships with Xfce and the &quot;Dev&quot; edition features the Cinnamon desktop together with a range of compilers and interpreters, including PHP and Rust. The project also produces a comprehensive &quot;Distro Building&quot; manual with a guide to the Archiso tool (for building custom Arch-based ISO images) and the Calamares system installer." href="helwan">Helwan</a> &bull; <a href="https://archive.org/download/helwan-linux-dev-lts-v-5.2-x-86-64/Helwan-Linux-Dev-LTS-v5.2-x86_64.iso">5.2</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-08</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="Infinity Linux is an Arch-based, rolling-release Linux distribution featuring the KDE Plasma desktop. Its primarily focus is on speed, flexibility, compatibility and ease of installation. The distribution uses the Calamares system installer and provides out-of-the-box support for Flatpak packages." href="infinity">Infinity</a> &bull; <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/infinity-linux/files/ISO/Infinity_Linux-2026.11.2-KDE-x86_64.iso">2026.11.2</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-07</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="Abora OS is general-purpose Linux distribution based on NixOS. It boots into a text-mode installation wizard that offers the user various options, including a choice of over 20 desktop environments, window managers and Wayland compositors, as well as several application bundles for a range of use cases. Some of the distribution's other features include out-of-the-box support for flatpak packages, Limine bootloader, command-line system management layer called ANIX, application management layer called TinyPM, and several custom Abora system management tools." href="abora">Abora</a> &bull; <a href="https://github.com/AnimatedGTVR/Abora-OS/releases/download/v4.2/abora-2026.11.07-x86_64-v4.2.iso">2026.11.07</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-07</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="AOSC OS an independently maintained Linux distribution based on the Linux kernel and various software components, using a custom package manager called oma which works with Deb packages for package management. AOSC OS is targeted at experienced Linux users and optimised for use on personal devices. It aims to provide a solid out-of-the-box experience, simplified system administration and a reliable work environment." href="aosc">AOSC</a> &bull; <a href="https://releases.aosc.io/os-amd64/installer/aosc-os_installer_20261107_amd64.iso">20261107</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-07</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="GhostBSD is a user-friendly desktop operating system based on FreeBSD. Its default desktop is MATE, but a separate community edition with Xfce is available too. It also features a selection of commonly used software, a rolling-release development model, and a bootable live image with an intuitive graphical system installer." href="ghostbsd">GhostBSD</a> &bull; <a href="https://download.fr.ghostbsd.org/releases/amd64/26.3.R15.1p6/GhostBSD-26.3.R15.1p6.iso">26.3</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-07</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="MODICIA O.S. is a Linux multimedia distribution designed primarily for musicians, graphic designers and video makers. It is based on Debian's &quot;stable&quot; branch, but uses the Cinnamon desktop and a recent Linux kernel. MODICIA O.S. comes with a set of carefully-selected, open-source multimedia software and tools, such as Audacity (audio editor), Brasero (disc-burning utility), Cheese (webcam application), Curlew (multimedia converter), GIMP (graphics editor), HandBrake (video transcoder), Kdenlive (video editor), MediaInfo (tool that provides technical data about media files), mpv (media player), Peek (animated GIF recorder), RawTherapee (photo processor), XnView (image viewer), and many others. The distribution also integrates the OnlyOffice software suite for general office tasks." href="modicia">MODICIA</a> &bull; <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/modicia-o-s/files/MODICIA-O.S.Caravaggio-6.12.115-RT-LTS-amd64.iso">6.12.115</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-07</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="HackerOS is a live Linux distribution based on Debian's &quot;Testing&quot; branch and designed for regular users, gamers and cybersecurity enthusiasts. Some of its features include an optimised XanMod Linux kernel for faster boot times and reduced resource usage, out-of-the-box support for NVIDIA graphics cards, and a collection of cybersecurity tools, such as enhanced firewalls and intrusion detection software. The distribution uses the KDE Plasma desktop." href="hackeros">HackerOS</a> &bull; <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/hackeros/files/OFFICIAL/HackerOS-V5.1.iso">5.1</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="News">11-07</th>
          <td class="News"><a title="SystemRescue is an Arch-based Linux system on a bootable DVD or USB drive, designed for repairing a system and rescue data after a crash. It also aims to provide an easy way to carry out administration tasks on a computer, such as creating and editing hard disk partitions. It contains many useful system utilities (GNU Parted, PartImage, FSTools) and some basic ones (editors, Midnight Commander, network tools). It aims to be very easy to use. The kernel of the system supports all of today's most important filesystems, including ext2, ext3, ext4, ReiserFS, Reiser4, Btrfs, XFS, JFS, VFAT, NTFS, ISO9660, as well as network filesystems, such as Samba and NFS." href="systemrescue">SystemRescue</a> &bull; <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/systemrescuecd/files/sysresccd-x86/13.03/systemrescue-13.03-amd64.iso">13.03</a></td>
        </tr>
      </table>
