        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px"><a href="partedmagic">Parted Magic</a> is a small live CD/USB/PXE with its elemental purpose being to partition hard drives. The project's latest version, 26.11, introduces support for computers running 64-bit ARM processors. "<span class="Quote">This release adds a second edition of Parted Magic for ARM computers, six new programs and Linux kernel 7.3. Erase verifies drives much faster and clears memory cards the way IEEE 2883 asks. Parted Magic now comes in a second edition for 64-bit ARM computers. Its ISO image sits beside the PC ISO in the downloads at no extra cost - everyone who can download this release can download both. It is made for ARM servers that start with UEFI and for Snapdragon X laptops, and it starts with Secure Boot on. I tested it on an Ampere Altra server and a Lenovo ThinkPad T14s Gen 6. It is not made for Macs or for boards such as the Raspberry Pi. It has Erase, VisParted, Clone, Rescue, Boot Repair and the other new programs below, with Google Chrome as its web browser. The USB Installer writes it to a USB drive. The ARM edition also has the USB Installer built in, so an ARM computer can make Parted Magic drives for PCs too.</span>" Further details on the 26.11 release can be found on the project's <a href="https://partedmagic.com/store/">news page</a>. Parted Magic may be purchased and downloaded through the <a href="hhttps://partedmagic.com/store/?ref=8">on-line store</a>.</td>
