</td>
        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px"><a href="capivaraos">CapivaraOS</a>, a Fedora-based Linux distribution with a choice of GNOME, KDE Plasma and Xfce desktop, has received a major update to version 2.0.0. Derived from Fedora 45, the new release promises continuous in-place upgrades and adds new custom applications: "<span class="Quote">Marsh, Pup and Snout 2.0.0 are available for download. Series 2 is not Series 1 with newer packages. It is a rebuild on Fedora 45, and almost everything you see has moved or been redone. Never reinstall again - this is the change that changes daily life the most. From Series 2 on, CapivaraOS upgrades in place - 2.0 to 2.1, and Series 2 to Series 3 when the time comes. No formatting, no reinstalling, no copying your files to another disk first. It works through Discover, GNOME Software or dnf, like any other update, because that is exactly what it is - our repository is signed and upgrades go through the same verification as everything else. And before each upgrade Snapper takes a snapshot, so rolling back is one command. Series 1 does not have this path. If you are on it, you need to install 2.0 from scratch - this is the last time.</span>" Continue to the <a href="https://www.capivaraos.org/en/blog-series2-released.html">release announcement</a> for more details. <a href="https://www.capivaraos.org/en/download.html">Download</a> (<a href="table.php?distribution=capivaraos&amp;pkglist=true&amp;version=2.0.0#pkglist">pkglist</a>): <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/capivaraos/files/CapivaraOS-Snout/2.0.0/CapivaraOS-Snout-2.0.0-x86_64.iso">CapivaraOS-Snout-2.0.0-x86_64.iso</a> (GNOME, 3,540MB, <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/capivaraos/files/CapivaraOS-Snout/2.0.0/CapivaraOS-Snout-2.0.0-x86_64.iso.sha256">SHA256</a>, <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/capivaraos/files/CapivaraOS-Snout/2.0.0/CapivaraOS-Snout-2.0.0-x86_64.iso.sha256.asc">signature</a>, <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/capivaraos/files/CapivaraOS-Snout/2.0.0/CapivaraOS-Snout-2.0.0-x86_64.iso.torrent">torrent</a>), <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/capivaraos/files/CapivaraOS-Marsh/2.0.0/CapivaraOS-Marsh-2.0.0-x86_64.iso">CapivaraOS-Marsh-2.0.0-x86_64.iso</a> (KDE Plasma, 5,106MB, <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/capivaraos/files/CapivaraOS-Marsh/2.0.0/CapivaraOS-Marsh-2.0.0-x86_64.iso.sha256">SHA256</a>, <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/capivaraos/files/CapivaraOS-Marsh/2.0.0/CapivaraOS-Marsh-2.0.0-x86_64.iso.sha256.asc">signature</a>, <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/capivaraos/files/CapivaraOS-Marsh/2.0.0/CapivaraOS-Marsh-2.0.0-x86_64.iso.torrent">torrent</a>), <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/capivaraos/files/CapivaraOS-Pup/2.0.0/CapivaraOS-Pup-2.0.0-x86_64.iso">CapivaraOS-Pup-2.0.0-x86_64.iso</a> (Xfce, 3,101MB, <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/capivaraos/files/CapivaraOS-Pup/2.0.0/CapivaraOS-Pup-2.0.0-x86_64.iso.sha256">SHA256</a>, <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/capivaraos/files/CapivaraOS-Pup/2.0.0/CapivaraOS-Pup-2.0.0-x86_64.iso.sha256.asc">signature</a>, <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/capivaraos/files/CapivaraOS-Pup/2.0.0/CapivaraOS-Pup-2.0.0-x86_64.iso.torrent">torrent</a>).</td>
