        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">David Heinemeier Hansson has announced the release of <a href="omarchy">Omarchy</a> 4.5.0, an updated build of the project's Arch-based Linux distribution with a customised Hyprland tiling compositor. This is the distribution's first release than can be installed on Apple's silicon range of processors. "<span class="Quote">Omarchy 4.5 is the first big feature release since Quattro, and it's a whopper - over 740 pull requests merged from more than 180 contributors in just twelve weeks. It now offers a traditional desktop mode next to the tiling default. You can install it natively on a M1/M2/M3/Neo MacBooks. And it speaks 50 languages. And a gazillion other features, fixes and improvements. Already on Omarchy? Run Update, Omarchy. New machine? Grab it here. Super + L now cycles any workspace between tiling, scrolling and floating. On a floating workspace, every window gets a titlebar in your theme's colors, and a dock shows your pinned apps, everything that's running, and a grid of every app installed. Drag to reorder or pin, right click for more, and Super + M minimizes a window down to the dock. This is a wonderful on-ramp for anyone arriving from macOS or Windows who isn't ready to go all-in on tiling yet. Or for anyone who just wants one workspace where windows can sprawl. Mix and match per workspace, and the bar shows which layout each one uses.</span>" See the <a href="https://omarchy.org/news/2026/11/omarchy-4-5/">release announcement</a> for more information and screenshots. <a href="https://omarchy.org/#install">Download (SHA256</a>, <a href="table.php?distribution=omarchy&pkglist=true&version=4.5.0#pkglist">pkglist</a>): <a href="https://iso.omarchy.org/omarchy-4.5.0-x86.iso">omarchy-4.5.0-x86.iso</a> (6,238MB, <a href="https://iso.omarchy.org/omarchy-4.5.0-x86.iso.sig">signature</a>), <a href="https://iso.omarchy.org/omarchy-4.5.0-aarch64.iso">omarchy-4.5.0-aarch64.iso</a> (5,790MB, <a href="https://iso.omarchy.org/omarchy-4.5.0-x86.iso.sig">signature</a>).</td>
