        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">The Artix development team has updated <a href="artix">Artix</a> Linux to stable version 20261102. Artix Linux is a set of Arch-based, systemd-free distributions with a choice of Cinnamon, KDE Plasma, LXDE, LXQt, MATE and Xfce desktops. The KDE Plasma variant wasn't originally deemed ready for the release, but it has now also appeared on the project's download server with a 20261104 version number. "<span class="Quote">Official ISO release 2026-11. Second official release for 2026. Post feedback at the forum announcement thread. Main release notes: Plasma has switched to Wayland and all related configuration for the Plasma and Community-Qt editions has been appropriately updated; user services have matured and been fully implemented for OpenRC and dinit, they can also be enabled for runit and s6 via userspawn, however, for the time being, this task is left to the end user; currently, only Plasma has full Wayland support, other desktop environments are in various stages of implementing it, but not yet ready for daily use - therefore, even if a Wayland session appears on the login manager, it probably will not work well if at all; the Plasma and Xfce gaming editions are still in beta status and shall remain in the weekly downloads section for further testing.</span>" Visit the project's <a href="https://artixlinux.org/news.php#Official_ISO_release_2026-11">news page</a> to read the brief release announcement. <a href="https://download.artixlinux.org/isos.php">Download</a> (<a href="https://download.artixlinux.org/iso/sha256sums">SHA256</a>, <a href="https://distrowatch.com/table.php?distribution=artix&pkglist=true&version=20261102#pkglist">pkglist</a>): <a href="https://mirrors.ocf.berkeley.edu/artix-iso/artix-cinnamon-openrc-20261102-x86_64.iso">artix-cinnamon-openrc-20261102-x86_64.iso</a> (2,268MB), <a href="https://mirrors.ocf.berkeley.edu/artix-iso/artix-lxde-dinit-20261102-x86_64.iso">artix-lxde-dinit-20261102